<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" id="defs_P_14_2" targetNamespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <process id="P_14_2" name="14.2 Manage skills and certification" isExecutable="false">
    <documentation>Four of the six processes are drawn. 14.2.4 assignment restriction and 14.2.6 span of control are DMN files this flow calls.

THREE RECORDS THAT LOOK ALIKE AND ARE NOT. A competency profile (14.2.1) says what a person can do. A certification (14.2.2) is a credential with an expiry somebody else set. A qualification (14.2.5) is an evaluated individual against an identified covered task under 49 CFR 192 Subpart N. Merging any two makes an unexpired certificate look like current competence, or a training attendance look like an evaluation, and 192.809 is explicit that the INDIVIDUAL is evaluated.

TRAINING IS NOT QUALIFICATION and the flow keeps them on separate paths that meet only at the record. A course delivered is evidence for the profile; only an evaluation qualifies anyone for a covered task.

THE ASYMMETRY. 14.2.5 and 14.2.6 are gas only, because Subpart N applies to gas pipeline operators and no federal qualification programme requirement exists for electric distribution workers - 16 U.S.C. 824o excludes local distribution. The electric branch reaches 1910.269(a)(2)'s qualified employee and 1926 Subpart P's competent person, and neither is a programme.

AND THIS GROUP QUALIFIES OPERATOR PEOPLE ONLY. Contractor qualification is 16.1.4's and must match 192.805 independently; a contractor's own assertion that someone is qualified is not an evaluation the operator holds.</documentation>
    <laneSet id="P_14_2_lanes">
      <lane id="l_142_train" name="Competence and training">
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_start</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_kind</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_gap</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_tr</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_prof</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_cred</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_warn</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_lapse</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_mark</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
      <lane id="l_142_qual" name="Qualification">
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_cov</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_task</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_eval</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_ele</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_pub</flowNodeRef>
        <flowNodeRef>n_142_end</flowNodeRef>
      </lane>
    </laneSet>
    <startEvent id="n_142_start" name="Competence is gained, assessed, expires, or a task is identified"><conditionalEventDefinition id="n_142_start_cd"><condition/></conditionalEventDefinition></startEvent>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_142_kind" name="Which record is affected"/>
    <userTask id="n_142_gap" name="Compare required competence against what is held"><documentation>14.2.3. The gap is what the training plan is built from.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_142_tr" name="Plan, deliver or procure the training"><documentation>14.2.3. Training bodies are not standards publishers - MEA EnergyU, NGA and SGA deliver courses on 49 CFR 192 and ASME B31Q; the authority is the regulation.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_142_prof" name="Record the competency profile and its evidence"><documentation>14.2.1. What the person can do. NOT a qualification.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_142_cred" name="Record the credential and its issuer expiry"><documentation>14.2.2. The issuer sets the expiry. An operator review date recorded as the expiry is how a licence lapses while the record says current.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_142_warn" name="Warn ahead of expiry with time to renew"><documentation>14.2.2. A lapse found on the expiry date is a person out of service that day.</documentation></sendTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_142_lapse" name="Renewed before expiry"/>
    <serviceTask id="n_142_mark" name="Mark the credential lapsed"><documentation>14.2.2. The lapse is a fact in its own right: 14.2.4 refuses assignment on it and 14.1.4 suspends the access that depended on it.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <exclusiveGateway id="n_142_cov" name="Gas covered task"/>
    <userTask id="n_142_task" name="Identify the covered task against the 192.803 test"><documentation>14.2.5. Gas only. No federal qualification programme requirement exists for electric distribution workers.</documentation></userTask>
    <userTask id="n_142_eval" name="Evaluate the individual and record the outcome"><documentation>14.2.5. 192.809 requires the INDIVIDUAL to be evaluated. Attendance at a course is not an evaluation.</documentation></userTask>
    <serviceTask id="n_142_ele" name="Record the electric qualification basis"><documentation>1910.269(a)(2) qualified employee, 1926 Subpart P competent person. A definition and a role, not a programme.</documentation></serviceTask>
    <sendTask id="n_142_pub" name="Publish the position to assignment and access"><documentation>14.2.4 reads this and restricts assignment; 14.1.4 reads it and revises access.</documentation></sendTask>
    <endEvent id="n_142_end" name="Qualification position current and published"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_start_n_142_kind" sourceRef="n_142_start" targetRef="n_142_kind" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_kind_n_142_gap" sourceRef="n_142_kind" targetRef="n_142_gap" name="competence gap or training demand"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_kind_n_142_cred" sourceRef="n_142_kind" targetRef="n_142_cred" name="credential recorded or expiring"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_kind_n_142_cov" sourceRef="n_142_kind" targetRef="n_142_cov" name="covered task or evaluation"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_gap_n_142_tr" sourceRef="n_142_gap" targetRef="n_142_tr" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_tr_n_142_prof" sourceRef="n_142_tr" targetRef="n_142_prof" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_prof_n_142_pub" sourceRef="n_142_prof" targetRef="n_142_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_cred_n_142_warn" sourceRef="n_142_cred" targetRef="n_142_warn" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_warn_n_142_lapse" sourceRef="n_142_warn" targetRef="n_142_lapse" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_lapse_n_142_pub" sourceRef="n_142_lapse" targetRef="n_142_pub" name="renewed"/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_lapse_n_142_mark" sourceRef="n_142_lapse" targetRef="n_142_mark" name="lapsed"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[renewed = false]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_mark_n_142_pub" sourceRef="n_142_mark" targetRef="n_142_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_cov_n_142_task" sourceRef="n_142_cov" targetRef="n_142_task" name="gas"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "gas"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_cov_n_142_ele" sourceRef="n_142_cov" targetRef="n_142_ele" name="electric"><conditionExpression xsi:type="tFormalExpression"><![CDATA[commodity = "electric"]]></conditionExpression></sequenceFlow>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_task_n_142_eval" sourceRef="n_142_task" targetRef="n_142_eval" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_eval_n_142_pub" sourceRef="n_142_eval" targetRef="n_142_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_ele_n_142_pub" sourceRef="n_142_ele" targetRef="n_142_pub" name=""/>
    <sequenceFlow id="f_n_142_pub_n_142_end" sourceRef="n_142_pub" targetRef="n_142_end" name=""/>
  </process>
